-- title:
--   Diamond operators on the function field of X_H(q²M'), q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a positive natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ over $L$ which is assumed to equal the base change [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $\mathsf q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of that field, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Then there exists a group homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ to the group of $L$-algebra automorphisms of $K$ with four properties. (a) Slash compatibility: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(q^2M')$, a weight $k\in\mathbb Z$, modular forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ of weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$, integral power series $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ over $\mathbb Z$ whose images in $\mathbb C[\![\mathsf q]\!]$ are the $\mathsf q$-expansions (at width $1$) of $f,g,f_1,g_1$ respectively, and a nonzero $c\in\mathbb C$ with $f_1=c\,(f\mid_k\gamma)$ and $g_1=c\,(g\mid_k\gamma)$ as functions on the upper half plane, and with the Laurent series $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_g)$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_{g_1})$ (the images of $p_g,p_{g_1}$ in $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$) both nonzero: every $x\in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_g)$ satisfies that $\rho(\gamma)x$ has underlying Laurent series $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_{f_1})/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_{g_1})$. (b) Each $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes every element of $K$ lying in the base change to $L$ of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $j(d\tau)$ for $d\mid q^2M'$. (c) Conversely, every $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ fixing that subfield pointwise is $\rho(\gamma)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(q^2M')$. (d) $\rho(\gamma)=1$ if and only if the unit [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units (q ^ 2 * M') γ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) determined by the lower-right entry of $\gamma$ modulo $q^2M'$ lies in the subgroup generated by `levelH q M'` together with $-1$.
--
--   This is the existence, slash description, fixed-field property and kernel computation for the diamond operators on the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ over a characteristic-zero base field, identifying the $L$-automorphism group of $K$ over the field of $X_0(q^2M')$ with $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times/\{\pm1\}$ via $\gamma\mapsto d(\gamma)$; it is the $q=3$ case of a statement whose conclusion does not refer to $q$ beyond the level. It feeds the construction of elements of the chart algebra with prescribed constant coefficients on the Igusa-tower leg of the argument.
